>how do you engrave with gems? I always just end up 'writing in the dust'.

Gems come in two varieties:  hard and soft.  If you try to engrave
with soft gems, you will end up writing in the dust.  If you use hard
gems, you will be able to actually engrave in the floor.

Hard gems include diamonds, sapphires, rubies, and emeralds, to name a
few.
Soft gems include all worthless pieces of glass.

(This is actually the method I use to decide whether or not to carry
gems around and identify them.  If they're hard, I usually identify
them and sell them/throw them to unicorns.  If they're soft, I
generally leave them behind.  This has some disadvantages:  most
notably, dilithium crystals, the most valuable gems in the game, are
soft.  However, such a vast majority of soft gems are worthless pieces
of glass, and all the really valuable gems other than dilithium are
hard, so I think that on balance it's worth it.)


